  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so there is no evidence to exploit and maximum uncertainty across all design dimensions. The most informative first step is to establish the simplest, most interpretable baseline: RNA-only with a single profile and PCA (n=2000) as the encoder. This anchors the search by quantifying what a minimal RNA pipeline achieves, providing the reference against which all multimodal and multi-profile configurations can be meaningfully compared. Without this baseline, a multimodal result would be uninterpretable—we could not decompose how much performance comes from adding image data, multi-profile aggregation, or learned encoders versus the RNA signal alone. Under a limited budget, this single experiment reduces the most uncertainty: it calibrates the performance floor and makes every subsequent comparison (image-only, multimodal, different encoders, different aggregation) interpretable. It is the logical foundation before exploring the richer configuration space."
}

